+# 文档交付与运行时迁移
+
+## Scope
+
+本文档更新 reader guide 对 promotion lifecycle 的说明. Reader guide 本身不拥有 runtime behavior, Module responsibility 或 persistent state.
+
+## Requirements
+
+### Runtime Migration
+
+同一次交付发布 promotion runtime migration. Operation 先验证 artifact, 再写 temporary baseline, 最后 commit tracked state. Expected failure 保留 prior tracked state, rollback failure 返回 structured recovery result.
+
+### Authentication Boundary
+
+Protected promotion 只接受已完成 access control 的内部请求. 可信身份来自 security authority Input; promotion 不评估或选择授权 policy, 不接受 caller 自报身份或 credentials.
+
+### Rollout Ownership
+
+外部 Main Agent 负责在发布前协调并确认 runtime migration rollout 完成. 该协调不是 non-test runtime Module, 不改变 persistence responsibility.
+
+### Complete Operation Contract
+
+`promote(inputPath)` 的 successful result 精确为 `{status: "succeeded", artifactId, trackedStateId, summary}`. artifactId 与 trackedStateId 采用 Promotion Runtime 的 non-empty identity 定义, summary 采用 Result Summary 的定义. Expected filesystem failure 精确为 `{recovered: false, failureCode, operation, priorTrackedState, baselineStatus}`. 除此处字段集合外, 失败值语义采用 Promotion Runtime. Rollback success 和 rollback failure 精确采用 Promotion Recovery 的公开结果. Caller 只观察 public results, 不暴露 private helper 或 intermediate bytes.
+
+## Design Rationale
+
+选择在同一次交付中更新读者指南和 runtime migration, 而不是先单独发布文档, 因为共享发布窗口可以减少迁移协调. 拒绝先发布文档, 因为读者说明会暂时领先于实际行为. 接受的代价是发布范围扩大, 并需要同时协调文档与 rollout.
+
+## ADR Evaluation
+
+### Persistence Decision
+
+Tracked persistence 延续 baseline-first order, 因而由现有 persistence decision 覆盖.
+
+### Security Decision
+
+Protected operation 复用现有 authorization policy, 因而不形成新的 security decision.
+
+### Other Decisions
+
+Caller-visible success, expected failure 和 recovery representations 复用 Promotion Runtime, Result Summary 和 Promotion Recovery 的公开合同, rollout 不改变 authority source.
+
+## Testing Decisions
+
+通过 public promotion lifecycle 测试 successful persistence, expected filesystem failure, rollback failure 和 no-partial-commit behavior. 文档链接另做静态路径检查.
